version³13³1ts³11100585890³1cache_oldmajor³119³1cache_oldauthor³119³1cache_diff_default_author³11³1revision³120³1text_default³1version³21³2ts³21100585890³2ip³2217.247.139.242³2name³2text_default³2data³2summary³3*³3text³3= The Non-Rules of this Virtual Place =

Since this place is about anarchism, it is expected that lots of anarchists will make changes here. Telling anarchists what to do is like herding cats, so please take these as well-meant suggestions setting a tone for the place.

First off, be nice to your fellow anarchists, anarchists to be as well as those who have already taken the red pill. We're trying to sell the AnCap idea here. You catch more flies with honey...

The structure should be as open to change as the content, though once there's a large structure, we'll need a site map, table of contents, and topic pages to organize it all. Changing the structure at that point will require more work. That said, if you reorganize things, do your best to avoid orphaning somebody's work. Make sure every page that used to be available via a link is <i>still</i> available.

Respect your fellow wiki maintainers. If somebody gets something wrong, like "2 + 2 = 5", go ahead and correct it, but matters of opinion are just that. If you disagree, put a link in the other person's piece to your rejoinder on a new page (or use the TitleTalk convention).

TitleTalk convention summary: If you want to discuss the contents of a page, do it in another page with "Talk" added to the first page's name. Put that link at the bottom of the page, as on this page.

To talk with one of the [[Contributors]], change the Talk page for their personal page.

NonRulesTalk
